// Package testing provides the test result type used by the Binate test runner
// plus stdout print helpers for test programs.
package "pkg/builtins/testing"

import "pkg/builtins/testing/sys"

// TestResult is the return type for test functions.  Empty means pass; non-empty
// is the failure message.  It is an alias for the *distinct* named type
// sys.TestResult, so a `Test*` function returning it is explicitly labeled — the
// --test runner keys on that named type, not on a bare `@[]char`, so a `Test*`-named
// helper returning a plain char slice is not picked up as a test.  The underlying
// `@[]char` is unnamed, so `return ""` / `return someCharSlice` still assign without
// a cast.  The canonical type lives in the lang-free pkg/builtins/testing/sys so
// pkg/builtins/lang's own tests can name it without a `testing -> lang -> testing`
// import cycle (testing imports lang, below, for Stringer dispatch).
type TestResult = sys.TestResult

// Print writes its operands to standard output with a single space between adjacent
// operands and no trailing newline; Println is the same plus a trailing newline —
// matching the retired print/println builtins byte-for-byte.  Each operand is a
// char slice (written verbatim) or any type implementing lang.Stringer (rendered via
// String()) — the same `*any` dispatch fmt uses, but bottoming out in lang's
// Stringer impls (int/uint/bool/float and user types) rather than re-implementing
// scalar formatting.
func Print(args ...*any)

func Println(args ...*any)
